# Application updates

Sources: `packages/web/src/shared/lib/updater.ts`, `packages/web/src/features/app-update/`, and `packages/electron/src/main.ts`.

- UI consumes the existing update state/actions rather than invoking Electron updater or service-worker internals directly.
- Keep checking, downloading, ready-to-install, installation, and errors distinct. Inspect current types rather than inventing a status.
- Preserve installation coordination and pending user work. A renderer reload and an Electron process restart are different lifecycle operations.
- PWA registration/caching is configured in `packages/web/vite.config.ts`; Electron packaging/update metadata is configured in `packages/electron/electron-builder.yml` and `.github/workflows/ci.yml`.
- When diagnosing an update failure, distinguish metadata, download, integrity, disk-space, and installation failures. Do not delete app data as a routine fix.
